        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "caa3fefb-bbde-549f-92b4-2b6f888b15a0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1964 French Grand Prix\n- Places: Rouen-Les-Essarts circuit, Rouen, France\n- People: Graham Hill, Jack Brabham\n- Companies: BRM, Brabham\n- Roles: racing driver, team owner\n- Topics: Formula One\n\nFacts:\n- The 1964 French Grand Prix, formally the L Grand Prix de l'A.C.F., was a Formula One motor race held on June 28, 1964, at the Rouen-Les-Essarts circuit in Rouen, France.\n- Graham Hill started the 1964 French Grand Prix from sixth position and finished second driving a BRM car.\n- Jack Brabham finished third in the 1964 French Grand Prix in the other Brabham.\n- Norman Graham Hill was born on 15 February 1929 and was a British racing driver and team owner from England.\n- Graham Hill was twice Formula One World Champion.\n- Graham Hill died on 29 November 1975.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
